{
 "id": "t_energy",
 "group": "thread",
 "num": 5,
 "title": "Fueling the Body: ATP",
 "subtitle": "From chemical bonds to glucose, mitochondria and muscle contraction",
 "lectures": "Lectures 2, 3, 4, 14, 15",
 "voice": "af_heart",
 "scenes": [
  {
   "lec": "Overview",
   "title": "Follow the energy",
   "img": null,
   "terms": [
    "Energy",
    "Glucose",
    "ATP",
    "Muscle"
   ],
   "start": 0.4,
   "tstart": 0.4,
   "tend": 1.49,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Every movement you make costs energy.",
     "start": 2.19,
     "end": 4.13
    },
    {
     "text": "This story follows that energy.",
     "start": 4.58,
     "end": 6.33
    },
    {
     "text": "From chemical bonds, to glucose, to **ATP**, to a muscle contracting.",
     "start": 6.78,
     "end": 11.21
    }
   ],
   "end": 12.31
  },
  {
   "lec": "L2 · Energy",
   "title": "Energy stored in chemical bonds",
   "img": null,
   "terms": [
    "Kinetic",
    "Potential",
    "Chemical bonds"
   ],
   "start": 12.31,
   "tstart": 12.31,
   "tend": 14.23,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Energy is the ability to do work.",
     "start": 14.93,
     "end": 17.12
    },
    {
     "text": "**Kinetic** energy is motion: heat, light, movement.",
     "start": 17.57,
     "end": 20.83
    },
    {
     "text": "**Potential** energy is stored.",
     "start": 21.28,
     "end": 22.84
    },
    {
     "text": "Food stores potential energy in its **chemical bonds**.",
     "start": 23.29,
     "end": 26.41
    }
   ],
   "end": 27.51
  },
  {
   "lec": "L2 · Reactions",
   "title": "Anabolic and catabolic",
   "img": "L2_10.jpg",
   "terms": [
    "Synthesis",
    "Decomposition",
    "Anabolic",
    "Catabolic"
   ],
   "start": 27.51,
   "tstart": 27.51,
   "tend": 29.04,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "**Synthesis** builds molecules. It's **anabolic**, and it takes in energy.",
     "start": 29.74,
     "end": 33.94
    },
    {
     "text": "**Decomposition** breaks molecules. It's **catabolic**, and it releases energy.",
     "start": 34.39,
     "end": 39.05
    },
    {
     "text": "Digestion is catabolic. It breaks carbs into glucose.",
     "start": 39.5,
     "end": 43.14
    }
   ],
   "end": 44.24
  },
  {
   "lec": "L3 · Carbs",
   "title": "Glucose, the preferred fuel",
   "img": "L3_04.jpg",
   "terms": [
    "Glucose",
    "Glycogen",
    "Triglycerides"
   ],
   "start": 44.24,
   "tstart": 44.24,
   "tend": 45.85,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Carbohydrates are the preferred energy source.",
     "start": 46.55,
     "end": 49.18
    },
    {
     "text": "**Glucose** is C six, H twelve, O six.",
     "start": 49.63,
     "end": 52.27
    },
    {
     "text": "The body stores glucose as **glycogen** in the liver and muscle.",
     "start": 52.72,
     "end": 56.36
    },
    {
     "text": "**Triglycerides** store twice the energy per gram, but carbs come first.",
     "start": 56.81,
     "end": 60.93
    }
   ],
   "end": 62.03
  },
  {
   "lec": "L3 · Enzymes",
   "title": "Enzymes speed up reactions",
   "img": "L3_06.jpg",
   "terms": [
    "Enzyme",
    "Activation energy",
    "Catalyst"
   ],
   "start": 62.03,
   "tstart": 62.03,
   "tend": 63.71,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Breaking down glucose takes many reactions.",
     "start": 64.41,
     "end": 66.79
    },
    {
     "text": "**Enzymes** make them fast.",
     "start": 67.24,
     "end": 68.7
    },
    {
     "text": "As **catalysts**, they lower the **activation energy**.",
     "start": 69.15,
     "end": 72.0
    },
    {
     "text": "Lecture 2 said catalysts speed reactions. Enzymes are the body's catalysts.",
     "start": 72.45,
     "end": 77.59
    }
   ],
   "end": 78.69
  },
  {
   "lec": "L3 · ATP",
   "title": "ATP, the currency",
   "img": "L3_09.jpg",
   "terms": [
    "ATP",
    "ADP",
    "Phosphate bond"
   ],
   "start": 78.69,
   "tstart": 78.69,
   "tend": 80.36,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Cells don't spend glucose directly. They spend **ATP**.",
     "start": 81.06,
     "end": 84.47
    },
    {
     "text": "ATP is adenosine with three phosphates.",
     "start": 84.92,
     "end": 87.69
    },
    {
     "text": "Breaking the last **phosphate bond** releases energy.",
     "start": 88.14,
     "end": 91.08
    },
    {
     "text": "ATP becomes **ADP** plus phosphate. That's hydrolysis.",
     "start": 91.53,
     "end": 95.8
    }
   ],
   "end": 96.9
  },
  {
   "lec": "L4 · Mitochondria",
   "title": "Mitochondria make ATP",
   "img": "L4_05.jpg",
   "terms": [
    "Mitochondria",
    "Cristae",
    "Muscle cells"
   ],
   "start": 96.9,
   "tstart": 96.9,
   "tend": 98.68,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "**Mitochondria** make most of the body's ATP.",
     "start": 99.38,
     "end": 102.42
    },
    {
     "text": "Their folded **cristae** add surface area for the work.",
     "start": 102.87,
     "end": 105.59
    },
    {
     "text": "They're abundant in **muscle cells**, which use the most energy.",
     "start": 106.04,
     "end": 109.34
    }
   ],
   "end": 110.44
  },
  {
   "lec": "L3 · Transport",
   "title": "ATP and active transport",
   "img": "L3_16.jpg",
   "terms": [
    "Active transport",
    "Sodium-potassium pump"
   ],
   "start": 110.44,
   "tstart": 110.44,
   "tend": 112.38,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "**Active transport** spends ATP.",
     "start": 113.08,
     "end": 115.16
    },
    {
     "text": "The **sodium potassium pump** is the classic example.",
     "start": 115.61,
     "end": 118.68
    },
    {
     "text": "It resets sodium and potassium after a muscle fires.",
     "start": 119.13,
     "end": 122.53
    }
   ],
   "end": 123.63
  },
  {
   "lec": "L14 · Contraction",
   "title": "ATP in the cross-bridge cycle",
   "img": "L14_10.jpg",
   "terms": [
    "Release",
    "Reset",
    "Rigor mortis"
   ],
   "start": 123.63,
   "tstart": 123.63,
   "tend": 125.61,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "In muscle, ATP has two jobs in the cross-bridge cycle.",
     "start": 126.31,
     "end": 129.88
    },
    {
     "text": "ATP binding makes myosin **release** actin.",
     "start": 130.33,
     "end": 133.5
    },
    {
     "text": "ATP splitting **resets** the myosin head.",
     "start": 133.95,
     "end": 136.63
    },
    {
     "text": "No ATP means no release. That's **rigor mortis**.",
     "start": 137.08,
     "end": 140.44
    }
   ],
   "end": 141.54
  },
  {
   "lec": "L14 · Energy",
   "title": "Three ways muscle makes ATP",
   "img": "L14_13.jpg",
   "terms": [
    "Creatine phosphate",
    "Anaerobic glycolysis",
    "Aerobic respiration"
   ],
   "start": 141.54,
   "tstart": 141.54,
   "tend": 143.41,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Muscle stores only a little ATP. It has to keep making more.",
     "start": 144.11,
     "end": 148.13
    },
    {
     "text": "**Creatine phosphate** is fastest. About 10 to 15 seconds.",
     "start": 148.58,
     "end": 152.51
    },
    {
     "text": "**Anaerobic glycolysis** makes 2 ATP per glucose, with lactic acid. About 30 to 40 seconds.",
     "start": 152.96,
     "end": 160.06
    },
    {
     "text": "**Aerobic respiration** in the mitochondria makes about 32 ATP per glucose. It lasts for hours.",
     "start": 160.51,
     "end": 167.41
    }
   ],
   "end": 168.51
  },
  {
   "lec": "L14 · Fiber types",
   "title": "Muscle fiber types and fuel",
   "img": null,
   "terms": [
    "Slow oxidative",
    "Fast glycolytic",
    "Myoglobin"
   ],
   "start": 168.51,
   "tstart": 168.51,
   "tend": 170.16,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "**Slow oxidative** fibers run on aerobic respiration.",
     "start": 170.86,
     "end": 174.5
    },
    {
     "text": "They're packed with mitochondria and **myoglobin**, so they're dark red. They resist fatigue.",
     "start": 174.95,
     "end": 180.07
    },
    {
     "text": "**Fast glycolytic** fibers run anaerobically. They're white, powerful and tire fast.",
     "start": 180.52,
     "end": 185.91
    },
    {
     "text": "Endurance training adds mitochondria. That means more ATP.",
     "start": 186.36,
     "end": 190.41
    }
   ],
   "end": 191.51
  },
  {
   "lec": "L14 · Fatigue",
   "title": "Muscle fatigue",
   "img": null,
   "terms": [
    "Fatigue",
    "Lactic acid",
    "Oxygen deficit"
   ],
   "start": 191.51,
   "tstart": 191.51,
   "tend": 192.53,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "**Fatigue** comes when supply can't keep up.",
     "start": 193.23,
     "end": 195.51
    },
    {
     "text": "Low ATP. An **oxygen deficit**. **Lactic acid** buildup. Ion imbalance.",
     "start": 195.96,
     "end": 201.53
    }
   ],
   "end": 202.63
  },
  {
   "lec": "L15 · Hormones",
   "title": "Hormones that control fuel",
   "img": null,
   "terms": [
    "Insulin",
    "Glucagon",
    "Thyroid hormone",
    "Cortisol"
   ],
   "start": 202.63,
   "tstart": 202.63,
   "tend": 204.17,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "**Insulin** moves glucose into cells and storage.",
     "start": 204.87,
     "end": 207.67
    },
    {
     "text": "**Glucagon** releases it from the liver.",
     "start": 208.12,
     "end": 210.07
    },
    {
     "text": "**Thyroid hormone** is the main metabolic hormone. It raises heat production.",
     "start": 210.52,
     "end": 215.35
    },
    {
     "text": "**Cortisol** raises blood sugar to resist stress.",
     "start": 215.8,
     "end": 218.64
    }
   ],
   "end": 219.74
  },
  {
   "lec": "Recap",
   "title": "Recap: the whole path",
   "img": null,
   "terms": [
    "Bonds",
    "Glucose",
    "Mitochondria",
    "ATP",
    "Cross bridge"
   ],
   "start": 219.74,
   "tstart": 219.74,
   "tend": 221.13,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Energy sits in chemical **bonds**.",
     "start": 221.83,
     "end": 223.73
    },
    {
     "text": "Digestion breaks food into **glucose**.",
     "start": 224.18,
     "end": 226.24
    },
    {
     "text": "Enzymes and **mitochondria** turn glucose into **ATP**.",
     "start": 226.69,
     "end": 230.25
    },
    {
     "text": "ATP powers pumps, and every **cross bridge** in your muscles.",
     "start": 230.7,
     "end": 234.52
    },
    {
     "text": "Hormones keep the fuel supply in range.",
     "start": 234.97,
     "end": 237.3
    }
   ],
   "end": 238.4
  }
 ],
 "duration": 238.4,
 "audio": "stories/t_energy.mp3"
}